# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): the governor's veto. A poke sets the living to factions 1 to 5 (faction 5 is not in the game in
# this save), so that five factions vote, and another poke makes faction 2 the governor. On the Unity Fusion Core proposal
# (a yea and a nay) the governor votes nay with one other against and three for: the proposal would pass, but it fails on the veto (the
# result box says so; make_resolution gives -2). Escape closes it. On the next proposal the governor alone votes nay: the others being all
# for it, the veto is dropped and it passes (this one is not closed, which would carry it out). The window's own votes are poked in (-1 yea,
# -2 nay; faction n's is at 0x6ff6d4 + 4n). The state regions are as in councwin_vote.scene.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
